{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Compassionate:</b> From the thirteen attributes he mentioned what he needed regarding his afflictions, as Moses did at the time of his prayer, for he did not mention רחום וחנון, nor ה' נוצר חסד לאלפים — and I have already explained the reason in its place. And David mentioned רחום וחנון ארך אפים ורב חסד. And he alluded to נוצר חסד לאלפים — and this is 'and the kindness of YHWH is from eternity to eternity upon those who fear Him.' And he alluded to נושא עון ופשע וחטאה — and this is 'not according to our sins has He dealt with us; according to our iniquities has He removed our transgressions from us.'" "And the meaning of רחום — that it is possible to arrange providence to guard His servant before harm comes upon him." "<b>Gracious:</b> to save him when he cries out to Him." "<b>And slow to anger:</b> to lengthen for him." "<b>And abundant in kindness:</b> that He not cut off His kindness."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 103, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:01.776211644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}